ces 2021-22; water requirement with the 2020-22 survey adjustment","unit":"Rupees per quintal; cubic metres of water per hectare","limitations":["Added for this edition. The study did not place these crops.","The study measured how much water farmers actually use; added crops carry an estimate built from the official requirement instead.","A support price is the floor the government sets, not what farmers received; the study used market prices for most of its crops.","The averages for each season include the added crops. The study's own crops keep the groups the study gave them."]},"fodder":{"label":"Fodder crops","formula":"area under fodder crops ÷ gross cropped area; water per hectare from the Water Productivity Atlas, adjusted by the region's actual-use factor","source":"Gujarat Directorate of Agriculture, land-use statistics; Water Productivity Atlas (IWMI and ICAR, 2024)","vintage":"Area 2019-20 to 2021-22 average; water 2019-20","unit":"Share of cropped land; cubic metres of water per hectare","limitations":["Not placed in the four groups: fodder is mostly fed to the farm's own animals, so its returns come through milk rather than market sale.","The water figure is one figure for all of Gujarat, adjusted only for the region.","The Atlas assumes the same fodder yield every year and in every district."]}}}